chineseRemainder -- Solve simultaneous congruences.
***************************************************

  * Usage: 
        chineseRemainder(L,M)
  * Inputs:
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of integers.
      * M, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of positive integers, which are
        relatively prime.
  * Outputs:
      * x, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, an integer x between 0 and the
        product of the entries of M minus 1 representing the solution of the
        simultaneous congruences x=L#i mod M#i.

Description
===========

Solves the simultaneous congruences x=L#i mod M#i.



+--------------------------------------+
|i1 : chineseRemainder({1,2,3},{3,5,7})|
|                                      |
|o1 = 52                               |
+--------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

This should be extended slightly to non prime integers.

Ways to use chineseRemainder:
=============================

  * "chineseRemainder(List,List)"

