invertBirationalMap -- Computes the inverse of a birational map.
****************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        invertBirationalMap(I,phi)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, defining the source variety
      * phi, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a row matrix over the ring
        of I with linear system defining the map.
  * Outputs:
      * a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, of a matrix with the inverse of the
        birational map and the ideal of its image.

Description
===========

Computes the inverse of a birational map.

+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i1 : K=QQ;                                                                   |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i2 : R=K[v,u,z];                                                             |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i3 : I=ideal(v^8-u^3*(z+u)^5);                                               |
|                                                                             |
|o3 : Ideal of R                                                              |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i4 : linsys=matrix {{u^6+4*u^5*z+6*u^4*z^2+4*u^3*z^3+u^2*z^4,v*u^5+3*v*u^4*z+|
|                                                                             |
|             1       7                                                       |
|o4 : Matrix R  <--- R                                                        |
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|3*v*u^3*z^2+v*u^2*z^3,v^2*u^4+3*v^2*u^3*z+3*v^2*u^2*z^2+v^2*u*z^3,v^3*u^3+2*v|
|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|^3*u^2*z+v^3*u*z^2,v^4*u^2+v^4*u*z,v^5*u+v^5*z,v^6}};                        |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|i5 : invertBirationalMap(I,linsys)                                           |
|                                                                             |
|                                                                             |
|o5 = {| -t_5t_6       |, ideal (t t  - t t , t t  - t t , t t  - t t , t t  -|
|      | -t_4t_6       |          4 5    3 6   3 5    2 6   1 5    0 6   3 4  |
|      | -t_5^2+t_4t_6 |                                                      |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                2   2                              2         |
|     t t , t t  - t t , t t  - t , t  - t t , t t  - t t , t t  - t , t t  - |
|      1 6   2 4    0 6   0 4    6   3    0 6   2 3    0 5   1 3    6   0 3   |
|     ------------------------------------------------------------------------|
|                                2   2                       2                |
|     t t , t t  - t t , t t  - t , t  - t t , t t  - t t , t  - t t )}       |
|      5 6   1 2    5 6   0 2    5   1    4 6   0 1    3 6   0    2 6         |
|                                                                             |
|o5 : List                                                                    |
+-----------------------------------------------------------------------------+

Caveat
======

Speed this up. Perhaps give as argument just phi in R/I. Does not check whether
phi is birational.

