parametrize -- Rational parametrization of rational curves.
***********************************************************

  * Usage: 
        parametrize(I)
        parametrize(I,J)
  * Inputs:
      * I, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, defining a rational plane
        curve C or rational normal curve
      * J, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the adjoint ideal of the plane
        curve C.
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note parametrizeConic: parametrizeConic, => ..., default value null,
        Option whether to rationally parametrize conics.
  * Outputs:
      * pI, a *note matrix: (Macaulay2Doc)Matrix,, a column matrix with the
        rational parametrization of C.

Description
===========

Computes a rational parametrization pI of C.

If the degree of C odd, pI is over \mathbb{P}^{1}.

If the degree of C even, pI is over a conic. So to get the conic apply *note
ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)ideal, *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)ring, to the
parametrization pI. If the *note Option: (Macaulay2Doc)Option,
parametrizeConic=>true is given and C has a rational point then the conic is
parametrized hence pI is over \mathbb{P}^{1}.

If the second argument J is not specified and degree of C is bigger than 2 then
J is being computed via the package AdjointIdeal.

If the function is applied to a rational normal curve it calls *note
rParametrizeRNC: rParametrizeRNC,.

If it is applied to a plane conic it calls *note rParametrizeConic:
rParametrizeConic,.



